", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bc1705a4e7e929c73ac6f0cf1fc02b90a07dc51c1288028f8f242b2a333a5db2","event_uuid":"49f5172b-cf0b-4291-95c3-4770f7e4f54b","position":{"commit_sha":"af12bc3b2697391d0b2e5631a46b010a02a303b9","position":"1788876695500320001-49f5172b-cf0b-4291-95c3-4770f7e4f54b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed for live P1 replication outage. Initial evidence from operator: CloudWatch rebar-gerrit-mirror-out-of-sync ALARM; Mirror Guard says GitHub tip static across 3 samples; Gerrit main=12acd6e18be760e9df83f049957dacf9983e8ff3; GitHub main=665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732. I will read replication_log around 2026-09-08 10:37Z first, then test deploy-key/auth, queue/missing-object, and mirror-fetch fallout hypotheses one at a time.","timestamp":1788876030369549001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Interim debugging evidence (Phase 1/2): replication_log shows the first auth failures at 2026-09-08T00:00:33Z and current failures still say `Cannot log in at github.com:22`; JGit is trying ssh-ed25519 key SHA256:jBCGL6vjKQfNJQjW9qs43uVpUp7Nfo/2Ygx3kgN7Rmk, which GitHub refuses. The live host/container mounted deploy key is SHA256:iJ7j98LfAGhV+gz4JpEOuCSDAAZUYR9FPuayfCSwW9c (`rebar-gerrit-replication-rotated-20260907`) and an in-container ssh -T to git@github.com succeeds with it. Working vs failing difference: ordinary ssh reads the rotated key from /var/gerrit/.ssh and authenticates, but the running Gerrit/JGit replication plugin continues using a stale in-memory old key. Object-store queue/missing-object is not the first failing mode: failures are pure publickey auth before push content transfer. Next minimal operational fix is restart only the Gerrit container to reload the mounted SSH key/config, then trigger replication start --all --wait and verify GitHub main catches up.","timestamp":1788876155555514001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Repair applied at 2026-09-08T14:03Z: restarted only the Gerrit container to reload the already-materialized rotated replication deploy key. Gerrit came back healthy (HTTP /login returned 302 by the third 5s probe) and replication plugin loaded. Then triggered `replication start --all --remote github --now --wait` via Gerrit SSH. Immediate verification: GitHub main now equals Gerrit main at cc3b80b4a084716c52194f40d98208f487c07e91; post-restart replication_log window has no publickey/auth errors. Continuing to verify Mirror Guard/CloudWatch and prevention/RCA details before close.","timestamp":1788876284850829001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA update: confirmed root cause is deploy-key rotation order, not object-store corruption. Rotation ticket auspicial-wily-warbler records `/rebar/prod/github-replication-deploy-key` version 3 -> 4 and old GitHub deploy key id 155914477 deleted after a single verification. Live evidence shows the file key was rotated/materialized at 2026-09-07T22:41:43Z with fingerprint SHA256:iJ7j98LfAGhV+gz4JpEOuCSDAAZUYR9FPuayfCSwW9c, but Gerrit/JGit replication kept trying stale key SHA256:jBCGL6vjKQfNJQjW9qs43uVpUp7Nfo/2Ygx3kgN7Rmk until Gerrit restart at 2026-09-08T14:03Z. Prevention in progress: TDD RED added tests/scripts/test_gerrit_replication_key_rotation.py (initially failed) proving setup-replication must tell operators to restart/reload before verification and retire the old deploy key only after replication_log confirms the old key is no longer used.","timestamp":1788876695500320001}],"created_at":1788875566628196001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Problem\nGerrit -> GitHub replication is stalled during the live P1 object-store outage. CloudWatch alarm rebar-gerrit-mirror-out-of-sync is ALARM and Mirror Guard repeatedly reports GitHub tip static across 3 samples. Gerrit main is 12acd6e18be760e9df83f049957dacf9983e8ff3 while GitHub main is stuck at 665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732.\n\n## Investigation plan\n- Read Gerrit replication_log around the stall start (~2026-09-08 03:37 PDT / 10:37 UTC).\n- Test suspects one at a time: rotated replication deploy key not loaded/reloaded; replication queue wedged by missing-object failures; fallout from mirror-fetch recovery.\n- Confirm whether refs/heads/main replication is configured and whether tickets branch is excluded or independently managed.\n- Fix the confirmed cause with minimal operational change. If code/infra source changes are needed, land them through Gerrit.\n- Trigger full replication using the Gerrit replication plugin command and wait for completion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] replication_log evidence identifies the first failing mode at the stall start.\n- [ ] The confirmed root cause is documented on this ticket.\n- [ ] Gerrit -> GitHub replication is repaired without touching Gerrit git data before snapshot when mutation is needed.\n- [ ] Full replication is triggered and completes or reports explicit per-ref errors.\n- [ ] GitHub main equals Gerrit main after repair.\n- [ ] Mirror Guard is green on its next run, or any remaining alarm lag is explained with timestamps.\n- [ ] Confirm whether the replication config includes refs/heads/tickets or only code refs.\n\n## Constraints\nNever use --force. Do not restart Gerrit or mutate Gerrit git data unless coordinated through the object-store incident. Snapshot before any repository repair. Keep downtime minimal.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/gerrit/setup-replication.sh","reason":"documents the operational deploy-key rotation/reload order so the old GitHub deploy key is not retired while Gerrit/JGit still has the previous SSH key cached"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_gerrit_replication_key_rotation.py","reason":"regression test pinning that setup-replication warns about Gerrit/JGit SSH key caching and orders restart plus replication verification before retiring the old deploy key"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"02c3cfce-c9ca-46dc-9439-cc9efe8b7103","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"81a2-ec2a-e374-4d76","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gerrit to GitHub replication stalled after object-store repair","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["db6d1bd8-b71f-41b0-816b-cbb7473c3bf4","c8dc2b30-1f7a-4913-891a-517ce56cc38f","02c3cfce-c9ca-46dc-9439-cc9efe8b7103","add782ed-51fc-4dfa-bdc5-453f6368c835","d1059555-4d07-4840-b1dc-7e878614f47d","582e7113-1310-4dca-947c-709f9197e890","5b45a8f6-fb6d-4b84-b816-9ad05c5c1595","604f26d1-f03e-4bab-98c7-621fa552b070","49f5172b-cf0b-4291-95c3-4770f7e4f54b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788876695500320002,"uuid":"4c0f9cdb-6752-4448-9036-3d86745996b7"}